# stackcone Solutions posts

When the user pastes a **problem statement** or asks for a **solution post**, produce a full **proposed solution** brief in `solutions/` — same visual system as `blog/` (charts, Mermaid diagrams, tables, SEO). The page should read like a technical proposal and implementation plan: how to architect, build, operate, and report. **Do not** frame it as work already delivered or cite Upwork (or any job board) as the source.

## Deliverables (always)

1. `solutions/{slug}.html` — **published page** (only public URL)
2. `solutions/md/{slug}.md` — markdown source for authoring (not linked, not in sitemap)
3. Update `solutions/solutions.json` — add entry with `"author": "Amar Kumar"`
4. Update `sitemap.xml` — add `<url>` for the new HTML page only
5. Run `python3 blog/apply_highlights.py solutions/{slug}.html` if the page has code blocks

**Slug:** lowercase, hyphenated (e.g. `wordpress-seo-multi-agent-pipeline`). Published HTML: `solutions/{slug}.html`. Source markdown: `solutions/md/{slug}.md` — **never** put `.md` next to `.html` in `solutions/`.

## solutions.json entry

```json
{
  "id": "{slug}",
  "title": "Outcome-focused title",
  "description": "Problem + approach in one sentence (under ~155 chars)",
  "href": "./{slug}.html",
  "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "dateLabel": "Month YYYY",
  "author": "Amar Kumar",
  "category": "RAG | Data | API | Mobile | Docs | Platform | Automation",
  "tags": ["3–6 tags"],
  "client": "Company name if mentioned — omit otherwise"
}
```

Omit `client` if no company named. **Do not** add `source` fields (no `upwork`, no job-board provenance).

## Article structure (required)

| Section | ID | Content |
|---------|-----|---------|
| Title + meta | — | H1; `<p class="meta">By Amar Kumar</p>` (no date on page) |
| Summary | — | 2–3 sentences: **proposed** outcome and approach (future tense / “would”) |
| Table of contents | `.toc` | All major sections |
| Scenario | `#scenario` | Use case pattern, platform, owner profile, scope — state this is a **proposed solution** |
| Problem | `#problem` | Pain points, why manual flow fails, YMYL/regulatory notes if relevant |
| Requirements | `#requirements` | Functional + non-functional bullets |
| Architecture | `#architecture` | Mermaid diagrams + optional `.pipeline` + `.chart-wrap--architecture` |
| Recommended stack | `#recommended-stack` | Table + **why this stack** (vs alternatives) |
| Agent / component design | `#agent-design` | Per-agent responsibilities, inputs/outputs, QA gates |
| Implementation plan | `#implementation` | `.impl-phase` blocks — **4–6 phases** with deliverables, risks, rollback |
| Reporting & ops | `#reporting` | Dashboards, APIs, alert cadence |
| Proposed deliverables | `#deliverables` | 5+ concrete artifacts the build **would** ship |
| Effort estimate | `#estimate` | Hours range, ongoing maintenance — indicative |
| Charts | — | **At least 3** Chart.js charts in `.chart-wrap` |
| Glossary | `#glossary` | Terms table |

Do **not** add a bottom-of-page CTA block (no “Contact us”, “Hire on Upwork”, or similar sales CTAs). Site nav and footer already link to contact.

## Shared assets (reuse — do not duplicate per post)

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `solutions/solutions.css` | Diagram cards, lightbox, `.impl-phase`, `.pipeline`, chart wrappers |
| `solutions/diagrams.js` | Mermaid render, fullscreen lightbox, zoom/fit, drag-to-pan |
| `solutions/icons/*.svg` | Lucide toolbar icons (loaded by `diagrams.js`) |
| `blog/blog.css` | Article typography, tables, TOC, CTA, **code token colors** |
| `styles.css` | Site chrome |
| `site-nav.js`, `script.js` | Nav + shared site JS |

**Icons in `solutions/icons/`:** `zoom-in.svg`, `zoom-out.svg`, `fullscreen.svg` (fit), `x.svg` (close), `expand.svg` (card fullscreen). Do **not** embed toolbar SVG strings in post HTML — `diagrams.js` references these files.

**Mermaid theme/config:** only in `solutions/diagrams.js` (`StackconeMermaidConfig`). Never `%%{init:...}%%` in post HTML.

## Path convention (`solutions/{slug}.html`)

All paths below are **relative from** `solutions/`. Do not use root-absolute `/…` paths (breaks local `file://` preview).

| Asset | Path |
|-------|------|
| CSS | `../styles.css`, `../blog/blog.css`, `solutions.css` |
| Favicon | `../favicon/dark-favicon.png`, `../favicon/white-favicon.png` |
| Logo | `../logo/stackcone.png` |
| Mermaid + diagrams | `diagrams.js?v={N}` — bump `{N}` when `diagrams.js` changes |
| Site JS | `../site-nav.js`, `../script.js` |
| Diagram fullscreen icon | `icons/expand.svg` |

Canonical / OG URLs always `https://stackcone.com/solutions/{slug}.html`.

