## Exact HTML — Mermaid diagram card

Use **`mermaid-pending`** (never `class="mermaid"` — Mermaid auto-scans that class before `diagrams.js` runs).

```html
<div class="diagram-wrap" data-diagram-title="{fullscreen title}">
  <button type="button" class="diagram-maximize" aria-label="View diagram fullscreen" title="Fullscreen">
    <img class="diagram-icon" src="icons/expand.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
  </button>
  <div class="diagram-body">
    <div class="mermaid-pending">flowchart TB
  classDef agent fill:#f1f5f9,stroke:#64748b,color:#334155
  A["Label line one\nLabel line two"]:::agent
  A --> B</div>
  </div>
  <p class="diagram-caption">{caption below card}</p>
</div>
```

Mermaid rules:
- Node labels: `\n` for line breaks (not `<br/>`)
- `htmlLabels` is configured in `diagrams.js` — do not add `%%{init:...}%%`
- Prefer `flowchart TB` + `sequenceDiagram`; avoid Mermaid `LR` for dense labels (use `.pipeline` instead)
- `diagrams.js` wires maximize button + injects one if missing

Lightbox (automatic via `diagrams.js`):
- Toolbar: zoom out, zoom in, fit to screen (`fullscreen.svg`)
- **Drag anywhere on the diagram stage to pan** (no pan toggle button)
- Keys: `+`/`−` zoom, `0` fit, `Esc` close

## Exact HTML — Chart.js card

```html
<div class="chart-wrap chart-wrap--architecture">
  <canvas id="{uniqueChartId}" aria-label="{plain-language chart description}"></canvas>
  <p class="chart-caption">{caption}</p>
</div>
```

Use `.chart-wrap--architecture` on the architecture/component map chart only. Other charts use `.chart-wrap` alone. Palette: `['#2563eb', '#7c3aed', '#db2777', '#ea580c', '#16a34a', '#0891b2']`.

